  "content": {
    "title": "Indiana Fever have filled 9 spots on 2026 roster. What's next?",
    "text": "Updated April 13, 2026, 8:34 a.m. ETThe Indiana Fever are rebuilding their roster around Aliyah Boston, Caitlin Clark, and Makayla Timpson.Indiana has re-signed key players Kelsey Mitchell, Lexie Hull, and Sophie Cunningham.The Fever are looking to add depth at the forward, guard, and wing positions through the draft and free agency.INDIANAPOLIS — The Indiana Fever are in the midst of reloading their roster for 2026.The Fever lost their rights to Kristy Wallace and Chloe Bibby in the expansion draft on April 3, so coming into the shortened free agency period that started last week, Indiana had just three players under contract: Aliyah Boston, Caitlin Clark, and Makayla Timpson.It was only three, but it was a strong base. And the Indiana Fever have signed six players to bolster their roster since then.Indiana agreed to terms with Kelsey Mitchell on a one-year, supermax deal worth $1.4 million, bringing the 2025 All-WNBA first-teamer and MVP finalist back to the Fever for her ninth season. With a healthy Clark in 2026, the two will be one of the most formidable backcourts in the league.Buy 2026 Indiana Fever tickets!Indiana re-signed Lexie Hull, a restricted free agent, to a multi-year deal. Hull is a good rotational player and part-time starter for the Fever, giving Indiana a strong defensive presence. The Fever also re-signed Sophie Cunningham, an enforcer-style player who averaged 8.6 points per game before she was sidelined with an MCL injury in August.The Fever then signed Monique Billings, a forward who played with Mitchell in Unrivaled and Clark at FIBA in the offseason, to a multi-year deal. Billings brings a strong presence as a nine-year veteran player, and spent last season with Golden State.The Fever also re-signed Damiris Dantas for depth behind Boston and Ty Harris, a Noblesville native, to back up Clark.That gives Indiana nine players with training camp starting in less than a week.So, going into Monday's WNBA draft and the remainder of free agency before training camp starts April 19, what else do the Fever need?Fever targets going into draft, remainder of free agencyAt this point, the Fever mostly need depth at forward, guard and wing.They could, first and foremost, use a stretch 4 — someone who can run the floor, have elite shooting at the rim, and a decent 3-point shot.There are some players in free agency that still fit that bill, including Rebecca Allen, who spent 2025 with the Chicago Sky, and Temi Fagbenle, who spent the 2024 season with the Fever before she was picked in the Golden State expansion draft in 2025. Indiana could also look to find depth at the small forward/power forward position in the draft, with TCU forward Marta Suarez and UCLA’s Angela Dugalic likely available at the Fever’s No. 10 pick, or potentially Tennessee’s Janiah Barker in the second round at No. 25.Suarez averaged a career-high 16.8 points in her final season at TCU, and she developed a 3-point shot over her five years of college basketball. She shot 37.3% on nearly six attempts per game this season, which could give Indiana additional lineup spacing.Barker shot 36% from 3-point range on four attempts per game, averaging 14.3 points and 6.6 rebounds.The Fever could also use another wing, and Dugalic could also work as a depth piece there as a small forward/power forward combo. She has size at 6 foot 4 and shot 50% from the field, 32% from 3-point range while coming off the bench for the Bruins. UCLA’s Gabriela Jaquez and Gianna Kneepkens have also been mocked to Indiana at No. 10 this season.At guard, Sports Illustrated and SB Nation mocked South Carolina’s Ta’Niya Latson to the Fever, while The Athletic and ESPN have mocked South Carolina’s Raven Johnson. Johnson, more than anything, would bring a strong defensive presence to the Fever backcourt. She was SEC Defensive Player of the Year, a rarity for a guard, while improving her 3-point shooting to 39%. The Fever could benefit from depth at point guard, especially considering their top three PGs were all injured last season, but the backup spot is already filled by Harris.Latson could fill the void as a backup shooting guard, playing behind Mitchell. Latson is a shooting guard/point guard combo — she played primarily at the 2 at South Carolina, but would have the ability to cover at point if necessary.How the draft goes for the Fever will likely influence how they fill out the rest of their roster. The Fever have five more spots to fill, including two developmental players.Chloe Peterson is the Indiana Fever beat reporter for IndyStar. Reach her at capeterson@indystar.com or follow her on X at @chloepeterson67. Get IndyStar's Indiana Fever and Caitlin Clark coverage sent directly to your inbox with our Caitlin Clark Fever newsletter. Subscribe to IndyStar TV: Fever for in-depth analysis, behind-the-scenes coverage and more.",
    "word_count": 800,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
